                        <additions>
                            <p>
                                <locus from="LCI" to="LCI" scheme="other"/>
                                <note>Upper left corner, in brown ink by a contemporary hand: Epitaph of Magnus Ladulås (<quote>Epythafium regis magni ladhalas</quote>), in the form of 20 leonine hexameter verses, beginning: <quote>Suecia suspria sublato principe plora</quote>; see <bibl>
                                        <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107617" type="short">Andersson (2017)</title>
                                        <citedRange unit="page" from="16" to="16"/>
                                    </bibl>.
                                    Upper right corner, in brown ink by a contemporary hand: <quote>1270 fundata est hic domus nostra. 1335 fundata est domus predicatorum</quote>. In brown ink by an Early Modern hand: <quote>A.21. Calendarium Historicum fratrum in Gråmunka kloster Stockholmia. B.B.</quote>  
                                    Bottom, in dark brown ink by a contemporary or Early modern hand: <quote>Sue</quote> and <quote>1290/3</quote>.</note>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <locus from="RCI" to="RCI" scheme="other"/>
                                <note>Bottom left corner, in black ink: <quote>S.W. 54</quote> (note by <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/102800">Sven Wiklander</persName>).</note>
                            </p>
                        </additions>
                        <bindingDesc>
                            <binding contemporary="true">
                                <p>Repaired in <date when="1954"/> by <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/102800"> Sven Wiklander</persName>. Brown-reddish leather over wooden boards.The leather was originally pink or red. Remains of this colour visible on <locus from="LCI" to="LCI" scheme="other"/> and <locus from="RCI" to="RCI" scheme="other"/>. Two leather straps fastened to the front cover with catch plates; pins on the back. Marks of rust on <locus from="LCI" to="LCI" scheme="other"/> and <locus from="1r" to="1r" scheme="folios"/> may indicate the manuscript originally was chained. One nail visible at bottom of <locus from="LCO" to="LCO" scheme="other"/>; one hole after a missing nail. <locus from="Spine" to="Spine" scheme="other"/>: Five raised double bands and endbands. <locus from="Spine" to="Spine" scheme="other"/>, stamped in gold: <quote xml:lang="sv">Gråbrödraklostrets kalendarium</quote>; bottom, stamped in gold: <quote>A 21</quote> (current signum).</p>
                                <p>Bound under the auspices of <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/100821">Kanutus Johannis</persName>, guardian of the Stockholm Franciscans (1484-92), according to <bibl>
                                        <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107619" type="short">Collijn (1917)</title>
                                        <citedRange unit="page" from="129" to="129"/>
                                        <citedRange unit="footnote" from="1" to="1"/>
                                    </bibl>.</p>
                                <p>
                                    <dimensions type="binding">
                                        <height quantity="310" unit="mm"/>
                                        <width quantity="235" unit="mm"/>
                                        <depth quantity="50" unit="mm"/>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </p>
                                <condition> The original leather is very worn. The front pastedown is medieval, the back pastedown is modern.</condition>
                            </binding>
                        </bindingDesc>
                    </physDesc>
