                        <msContents>
                            <textLang mainLang="la"/>
                            <msItem>
                                <locus from="1r" to="1v" scheme="folios"/>
                                <title type="desc">Necrology and Memorial Book of the Stockholm Franciscans</title>
                                <msItem>
                                    <locus from="1r" to="1v" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <title type="uniform">Summary of the contents of the book</title>
                                    <rubric>Ianuarius</rubric>
                                    <incipit>Cristoferus rex Swecie</incipit>
                                    <explicit>Consecratus est nobilis dominus magister Iohannes in archiepiscopum</explicit>
                                    <finalRubric>Iulius</finalRubric>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem>
                                    <locus from="1v" to="2r" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <author>
                                        <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/100821">
                                            Knut (Kanutus)
                                            Johansson (Johannis)</persName>
                                    </author>
                                    <title type="desc">Verses by Kanutus Johannis, guardian of the Stockholm Franciscans</title>
                                    <msItem>
                                        <locus from="1v" to="2r" scheme="folios"/>
                                        <title type="desc">Panegyrical verses to Archbishop Jakob Ulvsson</title>
                                        <rubric>Recommendacio oratoria in laudem et extollenciam reverendissimi in christo patris et domini domini Iacobi diuina miseracione dignissimi archiepiscopi vpsalensis composita per fratrem Kanutum Iohannis sacre theologie baccalaureum ordinisque minorum quondam custodem et gardianum Stokholmensem anno domini 1490 in crastino beatissime matris nostre Birgitte</rubric>
                                        <incipit>Presulis ad tanti culmen vix ora venire</incipit>
                                        <explicit>Angelicus veniat te saciare cibus</explicit>
                                    </msItem>
                                    <msItem>
                                        <locus from="2r" to="2r" scheme="folios"/>
                                        <title type="uniform">Memorial verses about events in the year of 1489</title>
                                        <rubric>Metra edita per fratrem Kanutum Iohannem</rubric>
                                        <incipit>mcd lux tribus ix quater ad tria Roma stat holmis</incipit>
                                        <explicit>ast annno pleno pro qua laus sit tibi steno</explicit>
                                        <note>On this verse, see <bibl>
                                                <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107620" type="short">Öberg (1973-1975)</title>
                                                <citedRange unit="page" from="613" to="613"/>
                                            </bibl> and <bibl>
                                                <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107621" type="short">Collijn (1919)</title>
                                                <citedRange unit="page" from="40" to="40"/>
                                            </bibl>.</note>
                                    </msItem>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem>
                                    <locus from="2r" to="54v" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <title type="desc">Calendar</title>
                                    <note>The Calendar starts with 1 January and ends with 5 August. Golden numbers are only noted until <locus from="21r" to="21r" scheme="folios"/> (17 March) and some dates are duplicated (for example 1-8 May on <locus from="30r" to="33v" scheme="folios"/>), see <bibl>
                                            <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107617" type="short">Andersson (2017)</title>
                                            <citedRange unit="page" from="10" to="10"/>
                                        </bibl>. </note>
                                </msItem>
                                <msItem>
                                    <locus from="2r" to="54v" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <title type="desc">Obits and annalistic notes</title>
                                    <note>
                                        <p>
                                            Obits (Franciscans and others) as well as annalistic notes recording events in the Franciscan Order in Stockholm and the Nordic countries, as well as events in the city and the wider political and ecclesiastical spheres. The notes cover e.g. city fires, royal elections and politics, ecclesiastical affairs, and papal elections. For example:</p>
                                        <p/>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="2r" to="2r" scheme="folios"/>: The crusade towards the Turks, the Jubilee Year, the inauguration of the St George statue in the cathedral of Stockholm, the translation feast of St Katarina in <placeName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/place/100101">Vadstena</placeName> on 1 August, and the stranding of a whale in <placeName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/place/100391">Roslagen</placeName> (<date when="1489"/>);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="2v" to="2v" scheme="folios"/>: City fire, plagues and flooding (1495); altercation with deadly outcome in <orgName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/org/100009">Strängnäs Cathedral </orgName> (<date when="1496"/>);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="3r" to="3r" scheme="folios"/>: The Crusade towards the Baltic provinces (<date when="1496"/>);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="7v" to="7v" scheme="folios"/>: Siege of Bohus fortress (<date when="1502"/>);</p>
                                        <p/>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="21v" to="21v" scheme="folios"/>: City fire (1407);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="22r" to="22r" scheme="folios"/>: Siege of Nöteborg (1348);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="35v" to="35v" scheme="folios"/>: Siege of Stockholm by Sten Sture the Elder (1502);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="45v" to="45v" scheme="folios"/>: Leonine hexameter verses noting the papal election of Alexander V (1409);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="46v" to="46v" scheme="folios"/>: Election of King Karl Knutsson (1448);</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <locus from="53v" to="53v" scheme="folios"/>: Papal election of Sixtus IV (1471).</p>
                                        <p/>
                                    </note>
                                </msItem>
                                <bibl>
                                    <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107617" type="short">Andersson (2017)</title>
                                    <citedRange unit="page" from="16" to="65"/>
                                </bibl>
                            </msItem>
                        </msContents>
                        <physDesc>
                            <objectDesc>
                                <supportDesc material="parchment">
                                    <extent>
                                        <measure type="textblockLeaves" quantity="52" unit="folios"/>
                                    </extent>
                                    <condition>Holes in the parchment, some of which have been repaired, for example on <locus from="11r" to="11r" scheme="folios"/>, <locus from="12r" to="12r" scheme="folios"/>. Smeared ink on some leaves. Erasure on for example  <locus from="11v" to="11v" scheme="folios"/> and <locus from="12v" to="12v" scheme="folios"/>, <locus from="33r" to="33r" scheme="folios"/>. Stains on the parchment. <locus from="19" to="19" scheme="folios"/>: a fifth of the leaf has been cut away at the bottom.</condition>
                                </supportDesc>
                                <layoutDesc>
                                    <layout columns="1">
                                        <locus from="2r" to="54v" scheme="folios"/>
                                        <dimensions type="written">
                                            <height min="200" max="200" unit="mm"/>
                                            <width min="155" max="155" unit="mm"/>
                                        </dimensions>
                                        <note>Guidelines in ink.</note>
                                    </layout>
                                </layoutDesc>
                            </objectDesc>
                            <handDesc>
                                <p>7v, 20r, 32v: Olaus Petri, see Andersson p. 11 and Grandinson 1933. Autograph by Kanutus Johannis. Three main scribes.</p>
                            </handDesc>
                            <additions>
                                <p>
                                    <locus from="2v" to="2v" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <note>In brown ink by an Early Modern hand: <quote>Capitulum</quote>.</note>
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <locus from="3r" to="3r" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <note>In brown ink by a contemporary hand: An obit has been changed from <quote>requiescat in pace</quote> to <quote>requiescat in piice</quote> (<quote>may he rest in tar</quote>), see <bibl>
                                            <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107617" type="short">Andersson (2017)</title>
                                            <citedRange unit="page" from="29" to="29"/>
                                            <citedRange unit="footnote" from="39" to="39"/>
                                        </bibl>.</note>
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <locusGrp>
                                        <locus from="7v" to="7v" scheme="folios"/>
                                        <locus from="20r" to="20r" scheme="folios"/>
                                        <locus from="32v" to="32v" scheme="folios"/>
                                    </locusGrp>
                                    <note>Obits added by <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/102799">
                                            Olaus 
                                            Petri</persName>. 
                                        <locus from="7v" to="7v" scheme="folios"/>, in black ink: <quote>Anno Domini 1550 in crastino conuersionis Pauli obiit Erasmus Petri senator Stocholmensis</quote>;
                                        <locus from="20r" to="20r" scheme="folios"/> in black ink: <quote>Anno 1550 nona die Martii obiit Hans Ericson senator Stocholmensis</quote>;
                                        <locus from="32v" to="32v" scheme="folios"/>, in red ink, a verse about the death of Engelbrekt Engelbrektsson:  <quote>C quater et semel M quater x si bis duo demam Est Englibertus Maii quarta luce peremptus</quote>. 
                                        On this verse, see <bibl>
                                            <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107623" type="short">Grandinson (1933)</title>
                                        </bibl>.</note>
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <locus from="10r" to="10r" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <note>Outer margin, in brown ink by a modern hand: <quote>Nicolai Allonis</quote></note>
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <locus from="15r" to="53r" scheme="folios"/>
                                    <note>A modern hand has noted the month in pencil in Swedish in the lower outer corner of every recto leaf.</note>
                                </p>
                            </additions>
                            <decoDesc>
                                <p>Main text in brown ink. Rubrics, days and numbers of the calendar mainly in red.</p>
                                <decoNote type="initials">
                                    <p>
                                        <locus from="2r" to="2r" scheme="folios"/>: plain initial <quote>KL</quote> in blue with red flourishing. <locusGrp>
                                            <locus from="15r" to="15r" scheme="folios"/>
                                            <locus from="18r" to="18r" scheme="folios"/>
                                            <locus from="24r" to="24r" scheme="folios"/>
                                            <locus from="32r" to="32r" scheme="folios"/>
                                            <locus from="40r" to="40r" scheme="folios"/>
                                            <locus from="48r" to="48r" scheme="folios"/>
                                        </locusGrp>: plain initial <quote>KL</quote> in alternating red and blue.</p>
                                </decoNote>
                            </decoDesc>
                        </physDesc>
